<p>NOTE:  Cali Realty Corp said its operating income per share for the first quarter of 1996 excludes a gain on the sale of rental property of $5,658,000, or $0.32 per share, and an extraordinary loss of $475,000, or $0.03 per sharel.</p>
<p>Extraordinary loss on early retirement of debt in the first quarter of 1996 of $475,000 is net of minority interest's share.</p>
<p>Funds from operations for both periods are calculated in accordance with the National Association of Real Estate Investment Trusts definition, as published in March 1995.</p>
<p>Weighted average shares outstanding to calculate funds from operations assumes conversion of 3,624,000 in 1997 and 2,751,000 in 1996 weighted average limited partnership units in Cali Realty LP to shares of Cali Realty Corp.</p>
